312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (In ancient Rome, the public baths steamed with the fresh scent of lavender. The Romans loved to be clean, and they tucked lavender into their bathwater and even their laundry, so their skin and clothes carried its fresh, calming scent. They loved it so much that the plant's very name remembers it: 'lavender' is said to come from the Latin word lavare, which means 'to wash.' Every time we say its name, we speak a little Latin from two thousand years ago! Long before anyone could explain why a calming, cleansing plant was good for tired bodies, the gift was already growing on the sunny hillsides, waiting in the garden for the Romans.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
