363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (A GARDEN IS ALIVE. Stand still in a garden for a minute and you will find it is not still at all. God did not fill His garden with dead, unmoving things; He packed it with life, from the tallest sunflower to the tiniest ant. Leaves drink sunlight, worms tunnel the soil, bees hum flower to flower, and roots sip water underground. This first unit we slow down to wonder at all that God-made busyness.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
